      "statusChangeID": "6ac61c6325f7b6e35b71a1d9",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Sorry, but this behavior is intentional and changing it would regress existing content in VRChat.\n\nIf a constraint has no sources, then there's no information available to it about how it should be positioned, so it falls back to not constraining its target transform. In your repro steps, before activating Freeze to World in step 2, it's actually possible to move the constrained transform around manually in the scene in the SDK while in play mode, since the constraint has no reference for what it should be constraining that transform to.\n\nThis matches how Unity constraints behave. A Unity constraint with no sources acts differently to a Unity constraint with a single empty source, and VRChat constraints are built to match this as closely as possible. This is important for automatically converting Unity constraints to VRChat constraints when avatars are loaded in the client, as it means we can benefit from the performance boost of VRChat constraints without changing how the avatar behaves.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
