      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} `If a constraint has no sources, then there's no information available to it about how it should be positioned` I would have assumed it would have the same behavior as setting all source weights to 0 - use the \"rest\" values.\n\nShould I open a new canny for the weird issue in \"update 2\"? I have no idea why it requires a third keyframe, it's exactly the same as the second, but if the second is removed (so longer animation \"0.033s\", but just 2 keyframes) it won't work.",
